          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "For an executor administering a deceased estate in Queensland, several law firms maintain offices and dedicated succession law teams across **Logan, Greater Springfield, Ipswich, and the Western Brisbane corridor**:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Western Corridor (Ipswich & Greater Springfield)\n\n*   **McNamara Law** *(Offices in Ipswich CBD, Springfield Central, and Brisbane CBD)*  \n    One of the largest and most established legal firms in the Western Corridor. They have a dedicated Wills & Estates team that regularly assists executors with Supreme Court probate applications, Letters of Administration, asset transmission (Titles Queensland), and managing complex estates involving businesses or family trusts.\n*   **Fallu McMillan Lawyers** *(Ipswich)*  \n    A long-standing Ipswich practice with extensive experience in succession law. They guide executors through each stage of administration, from advertising and applying for probate to liaising with asset holders and distributing to beneficiaries.\n*   **Keane Legal** *(Ipswich & Brookwater)*  \n    Positioned conveniently along the corridor between Ipswich and Greater Springfield. They focus heavily on succession law, advising executors on personal liabilities, filing grants, and navigating intestacy issues.\n*   **Jacaranda Law** *(Ipswich)*  \n    A boutique practice focusing primarily on wills, probate, and deceased estate administration, making them well-suited for executors seeking a dedicated, smaller firm approach.\n*   **Richard Zande & Associates** *(Ipswich)*  \n    An established local practice (operating in the Ipswich area for over 60 years) with a strong probate and executor advisory footprint.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Logan & South Corridor\n\n*   **SKC Lawyers** *(Logan)*  \n    Focuses on estate administration and litigation. They assist executors with the formal probate process, tax compliance oversight, transmission applications, and shielding executors from personal liability during distribution.\n*   **Ryder Lawyers** *(Logan City & Ipswich)*  \n    Specialises in estate administration, probate grants, and beneficiary negotiations across both Logan and the Western Corridor.\n*   **Turner Freeman Lawyers** *(Offices in Logan Central and Ipswich)*  \n    A larger firm with dedicated estate administration lawyers in both Logan and Ipswich. They are suitable if the estate involves contested will issues, complex creditor claims, or potential Family Provision litigation.\n*   **Bennett Carroll Solicitors** *(Upper Mount Gravatt, Brisbane, and Ipswich)*  \n    Well-positioned to service clients between Logan and the Western Corridor, assisting executors with Supreme Court applications, asset transfers, and probate.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Brisbane Western Link (Milton to Forest Lake)\n\n*   **Lake Law (formerly Forest Lake Lawyers)** *(Forest Lake)*  \n    Strategically positioned right in the junction between southwest Brisbane, Logan, and Ipswich. They offer personalized, local assistance with probate applications, title transmissions, and estate settlements.\n*   **Will and Estate Lawyers Australia** *(Milton)*  \n    Located at the city fringe of Brisbane's inner west, they offer dedicated probate and deceased estate administration services (often providing fixed-fee arrangements for probate applications) across South East Queensland.\n\n---\n\n### Key Questions to Ask When Selecting a Firm\n\n1. **Fee Structure:** For grants of probate or letters of administration, many Queensland firms offer a **fixed-fee quote** for standard applications, while ongoing estate administration (calling in assets, paying debts, tax filings, distribution) is typically billed hourly.\n2. **QLS Accredited Specialist:** If the estate involves business structures, discretionary trusts, foreign assets, or potential family disputes, consider asking if an **accredited specialist in succession law** will oversee your matter.\n3. **Property/Title Experience:** If the estate contains real property in Logan or Ipswich, confirm whether their office handles the **Titles Queensland transmission applications** in-house to streamline the process.",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
